    "title": "Tyson Fury - News, Record & Stats, Next Fight & Tickets",
    "text": "Profile & Record Next fight News Results Potential fights Stream Tickets Discuss Stats Full record Ranking @ Heavyweight Tyson Fury profile What is Tyson Fury's Record? Tyson Fury's record currently stands at 35 wins, 2 losses, and 1 draw. Of those 35 wins, he has stopped 24 of his opponents, so his current knock-out ratio is 69%. Despite his 2 losses, he has never been stopped. He's boxed a total of 266 rounds, meaning his professional fights last 7 rounds on average. When was his last fight and how active is he? Tyson Fury's last fight took place against Arslanbek Makhmudov on April 11, 2026, in London, United Kingdom. He won by unanimous decision after 12 rounds. That fight was 5 days ago. Fury's last 5 fights have come over a period of 3 years, 11 months and 19 days, which means he has been fighting approximately every 9 months and 16 days. In those fights, he fought a total of 50 rounds, meaning that they have lasted 10 rounds on average. How Old Is Tyson Fury And Where Is he From? The heavyweight is currently 37 years old. He was born on August 12, 1988, so he will turn 38 in 3 months and 27 days. Fury was born in the United Kingdom. How long has Fury been fighting? Tyson Fury made his professional debut in December 2008, so he has been a pro for 17 years and 4 months. How good is he? Fury is currently ranked 3rd by The Ring and 4th by Box.Live at Heavyweight. How tall is Fury, What is his Reach And Which Stance Does he Use? Fury is 6' 9\" tall, which is 206cm. His reach is 85 inches, which is 216 cm. Fury fights from a traditional orthodox stance, which means he favours his right hand as his power hand when fighting. What are some potential opponents for Tyson Fury? Some potential future fights for Fury include Anthony Joshua, Unified Heavyweight Champion Oleksandr Usyk, Moses Itauma, Fabio Wardley and Jon Jones. What will be Tyson Fury's Next Fight And Where Can I Watch It? Tyson Fury doesn't currently have a fight scheduled. Some potential future fights for Fury include Anthony Joshua, Unified Heavyweight Champion Oleksandr Usyk, Moses Itauma, Fabio Wardley and Jon Jones. In the UK you can usually stream Fury's fights on Netflix. In the US you can usually stream Tyson Fury's fights via Netflix. What are some recent Tyson Fury results? Fury has beaten 3 of his last 5 opponents, stopping 1 of them, going the distance twice. In his last fight, he won against Arslanbek Makhmudov on April 11, 2026, by unanimous decision in their 12 round contest at Tottenham Hotspur Stadium, London, United Kingdom. Prior to that, he had been beaten by Oleksandr Usyk on December 21, 2024, by unanimous decision in their The Ring Heavyweight, WBO World Heavyweight, WBC World Heavyweight and WBA Super World Heavyweight championship fight at Kingdom Arena, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia. Going into that contest, he had lost to Oleksandr Usyk on May 18, 2024, by split decision in their WBC World Heavyweight, WBO World Heavyweight, WBA Super World Heavyweight and IBF World Heavyweight championship fight at Kingdom Arena, Riyadh. Before that, he had won against Francis Ngannou on October 28, 2023, by split decision in their 10 round contest at Riyadh. He had beaten Derek Chisora on December 3, 2022, by technical knockout in the 10th round in their WBC World Heavyweight championship fight at Tottenham Hotspur Stadium, London, United Kingdom. Tyson Fury Stats AgeDate Of BirthNationalityHeightReachStanceWeight Division 37August 12, 1988United Kingdom206 cm216 cmorthodoxHeavyweight (200+ lb) Tyson Fury Record Professional RecordWinsWins By KOKnockout PercentageLossesLosses By StoppageDrawsPro RoundsDebut 35-2-1352469%2012662008 Tyson Fury Rankings WeightThe Ring MagazineWBCIBFWBAWBO Heavyweight3---- Tyson Fury Recent Contests DateOpponentResultReplayVenue 2026-04-11Arslanbek MakhmudovWon (UD 12)Tottenham Hotspur Stadium, London, United Kingdom2024-12-21Oleksandr UsykLost (UD 12) watch replay Kingdom Arena, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia2024-05-18Oleksandr Us